            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "90. If an employee is called to work on what would otherwise have been a regularly scheduled day off and if the Employer fails to give one (1) hour's notice before the start of the required shift, the employee shall be paid for the hours of work actually performed plus one (1) hour, but is to be paid not less than three (3) hours nor more than eight (8) hours of pay in any one shift unless the employee works more than eight (8) hours in that shift.",
